cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use z-fasta, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "z-fasta"
abstract: >-
  Lightning FASTA work without the toolchain sprawl. z-fasta is a single
  static executable, written in Zig, that indexes, extracts, validates, and
  summarizes uncompressed FASTA files. It builds a compact binary index
  (.zfi) that supports any line layout, including mixed widths and blank
  lines, and emits a samtools-compatible .fai for uniformly wrapped files.
  Extraction serves positional regions, name lists, and BED intervals, with
  strand-aware reverse complement. Validation checks structure, identifiers,
  alphabet, and layout in one streaming pass with flat memory, compares a
  file with its index, and writes a repaired copy. Statistics report Nx,
  quartiles, and sequence composition through a bounded scan. Every failure
  carries a stable error code in text or JSON, and the same rules are
  available to other Zig programs as a package. Correctness is checked
  against samtools, bedtools, SeqKit, and other peers on human genome,
  transcriptome, and proteome datasets.
authors:
  - family-names: "Ergin"
    given-names: "Enes Kemal"
version: "0.4.1"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/eneskemalergin/z-fasta"
url: "https://github.com/eneskemalergin/z-fasta/wiki"
keywords:
  - FASTA
  - bioinformatics
  - sequence index
  - samtools faidx
  - Zig
